Answer: The ternary operator can select between integer values based on a condition.

```java
int A = 20;
int b = 30;
int c = 40;
System.out.println(A > 18 ? b : c);
```

Since A is 20, the condition A > 18 is true, so 30 is printed. Output: 30 If A is changed to 12, the condition becomes false and 40 is printed.

