All these values are within the valid range of byte.

Answer: The four variables using byte, short, int, and long, with each variable assigned the maximum value supported by its type.

```java
public class Demo {
public static void main(String[] args) {
byte A = 127;
short B = 32767;
int C = 2147483647;
long D = 9223372036854775807L;
System.out.println(A);
System.out.println(B);
System.out.println(C);
System.out.println(D);
}
}
```

The program demonstrates that different integer data types provide different storage capacities and value ranges.
